Evaluation scripts (data/scripts/eval)
======================================

These scripts turn the raw run logs in data/raw_data/ into the LaTeX table /
figure fragments under figs/. They share helpers from ../common.py, including
SERVER_TO_USE, which selects the data-collection server (gcpm1 / jet1tb) for
all server-specific logs. Run each from this folder (python3 <name>.py); each
prints the path it wrote.


RUNALL.sh
---------
Driver: runs every generator below, then check_data_server.py last. A failing
generator (e.g. a dataset whose real dump is still regenerating) is reported
but does not stop the run; the exit code is the number of failed generators.
Usage: bash RUNALL.sh


Python files
------------
datasets.py           Table 1 (tab:datasets): the Mal/Dna/Dlp dataset rows --
                      corpus size, document count, and regex-set size, measured
                      live from the source corpora and rule sets.

effectiveness.py      Section 7.3: the approximation-effectiveness tables
                      (pair-level + by-file-size), from the tier-discharge dump
                      any_server/eval_effective.txt.

gen_lkup_info.py      Section 7.4 (tab:lkup): lookup-table composition -- the
                      five lookup categories x three datasets, from
                      any_server/lookup_stats.dat.

gen_component_cost.py Section 7.4 (tab:component-cost): per-circuit cost profile
                      (R1CS per input byte, split across CP/SDE/DFA/framework
                      tiers). Needs a COST-instrumented dump; a dataset without
                      one yet gets a single "***" placeholder row.

gen_overall_perf.py   Section 7.5 (overall_perf.tex): stage-level performance
                      breakdown (select / commit / fold and compression parts)
                      per dataset.

gen_scale_all.py      Section 7.5 (fig:scale-regex): regex-set scalability
                      figure -- per-step circuit size and proof time vs the
                      fraction of the regex set, from the any_server scale
                      bundle (scale_data_gdb.tgz).

dna_reef_bora.py      Table 3 (tab:dna-reef-bora): Reef per-bucket cost vs BORA
                      on chr17 x NCBI, with the Reef-log parser reused by the
                      comparison generators.

gen_zombie_table.py   Section 7.7: two Zombie tables -- measured per-length
                      totals (+ derived unit cost) and the unit-cost projection
                      vs BORA across datasets.

gen_compare_all.py    tab:compare-all: the consolidated main-body comparison of
                      Zombie / Reef / BORA across all three datasets plus BORA's
                      speedup over each (reuses the Table 1/3/4 extractors).

count_loc.py          Implementation/eval: counts author-owned Rust lines in
                      new_zkregplus by module (vendored/upstream code excluded).

extract_acc_state_rate.py
                      Off-path analysis tool, not run by RUNALL.sh: the
                      AC-DFA accepting-state density rho behind the "sparse
                      match locations" remark (Complexity, Section 6.4).  It
                      writes no LaTeX fragment -- it prints a per-dataset
                      summary.  Its input, any_server/dump_acc_state_ratio.txt,
                      is not shipped; regenerate it first (see the recipe in
                      the script docstring and zkp_driver.rs:8748-8753).

check_data_server.py  Data-provenance check (run last by RUNALL.sh): verifies
                      every file under raw_data/{gcpm1,jet1tb} was collected on
                      the matching server (config-dump RAM is authoritative),
                      and that each *.tgz member's self-reported task matches the
                      archive name. Reports violations / unknowns / task
                      mismatches; does not write to figs/.
